I've a set of Aryas, Focal Clears, Anandas and several others.
I invested in some decent amps.
Even an EQ. Then I just bought some tower speakers, a center, and a sub from Dayton Audio.
I'd never heard of em, but I asked around with the budget audiophile folks, and decided to get them.
I got a Denon receiver. Nothing fancy.
Nothing about this setup is fancy. But they just sound better than my headphones. All of em.
